A||||8||Cozmo||Animals and Fieros???||||10||
Z||000000||Cozmo||06-23-2001||08:22 AM||||Reading about Fieros being dog toys  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008310.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/008310.html</A>   got me to thinking about Fieros and animals in general...<BR>When I park the white coupe and the black GT next to each other in the driveway and come back 24 hrs. later here's usually what I'll find...<BR>The white coupe will have cat tracks all over it.  If the windows were left open, cat hairs on the seats too.<BR>The black GT will have bird poop on it. A LOT of bird poop.<P>The cat thing I think I get. It's hot in Florida and the black GT turns into a rotisserie after being in the sun for a while. The white coupe is probably a much more appealing thing to lay on (BTW, I love cats). <BR>Now this bird excrement situation is different. I know, bird poop shows up much more on a black car VS. a white one, but I checked! As far as "strikes per square foot" the black GT has double the amount of poop than the white coupe.  I've even swapped the cars' normal parking spots with no real change in the results, so it's probably not the spot but actually the car.<BR>I don't know about this...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> ...<BR>So what about your Fieros' encounters with the Wild Kingdom???<BR>(I can hear the strains of the theme from "National Geographic" playing in the background)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><B>C02M0</B> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||stsmithgt||06-23-2001||04:23 PM||||I try to avoid parking under or near power lines, trees and light poles.  Especially if the sunroof is off. My cars is white, but there good at hitting the windows where it really stands out. <I>SPAT!</I> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>------------------<BR>My work of art.(in progress.)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||06-23-2001||04:45 PM||||here's the only animal that goes near my car.....of course, when he does it means a trip through a drive-thru for french fries for him!!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-246f.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>                  <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/3GTS_SIG.gif">                   </A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||skitime||06-23-2001||10:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cozmo:<BR><B>The white coupe will have cat tracks all over it.  If the windows were left open, cat hairs on the seats too.<BR>The black GT will have bird poop on it. A LOT of bird poop.<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>[b]C02M0</B> [/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Maybe the cat is protecting the car from the birds or the birds are trying to hit the cat and miss while hitting the black Fiero.<BR><P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pictures-1_5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pontiaddict||06-24-2001||03:26 AM||||I think the shiney black makes the birds think of water and with our swimming pool, birds tend to aim for it. I've heard they do so as a way of marking bad water. And since your car isn't water, it would be bad water.<BR>Or it's just sick twisted bird humor.||||reg||1
