Z||000006||84Bill||06-24-2001||12:16 PM||||Heheh Thats funny because my neighbors cat seems to like sleeping on my seats too. He seems to prefer the Indy over my 84SE and if neither are available he can usually be found crashed out on the drivers seat of my 88  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000007||Tigger||06-24-2001||10:47 PM||||My orange cat loves my Fiero (maybe because my Fiero is orange, dunno).  She likes to sneak outside at times, and when she does, all I have to do is open one of the doors and she hops in, makes it easy for me to catch her.  She purrs like crazy whenever around it, loves the seats and likes to curl up in the footwells.  I've been suprised a couple times to find her sleeping in it when the windows were left down.||||reg||7
Z||000008||Jaygee79||06-24-2001||10:52 PM||||I found Josh's (88CoupeV6) cat sleeping on my driver's seat once.  Another time we pulled up to his house and had just opened the door to get out and she came running and jumped into the car, so we took her for a little ride.  She was all over the place though.  Looking out the window, under my feet as I was driving, etc.  There's been a few times that I've come out of the house and saw the stray cat that lives in my yard sitting on my sunroof.  <P>------------------<BR>Jaime<BR>84SE red<BR>AOL IM: Jaygee79<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/jaygee79/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Jaygee79's Web Page</A><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pooheey1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
